SUMMARY:The Body of the Golem: A Life in Portraiture
DESCRIPTION:Artist and writer Riva Lehrer brings together portraiture\, Jewish tradition\, disability\, and the figure of the golem for the 2026 Phyllis Freed Sollod Memorial Lecture in the Mountain View Room of the Sherrill Center. Through art and storytelling\, Lehrer explores who gets labeled “monstrous\,” who has the power to define that label\, and what becomes possible when people claim their own bodies and identities. This lecture is sponsored by the Center for Jewish Studies. \nThe event is free and open to the public. \nAccessibility\nUNC Asheville is committed to providing universal access to all of our events. If you have any questions about access or would like to request reasonable accommodations that will facilitate your full participation in the film screenings\, please contact Stephanie Bullick\, Director of Accessibility\, at accessibility@unca.edu. \nVisitor Parking\n\nAll visitors must adhere to the University’s parking policy. Please visit the UNC Asheville Visitor Parking Permit Registration site to acquire a visitor permit to park on campus.
URL:https://www.unca.edu/event/the-body-of-the-golem-a-life-in-portraiture/
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.unca.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Event_Calendar_-_TEMPLATE_74.png
END:VEVENT
